    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, who leads today\u2019s charge with a stellar 81.24 efficiency score. The matchup against Elder is ideal; the combination of a favorable SP_xERA (4.40) and **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s elite sprint speed creates a prime opportunity to capitalize on our league\u2019s scarcest category: stolen bases. Joining him as a top-tier play is **Max Muncy**, who benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the soft matchup against Cody Bradford. Despite hitting in the seven-hole, **Max Muncy**\u2019s projected park environment and the favorable platoon advantage make him a high-floor start today, while **Josh Naylor** and **Mickey Moniak** both clear the 63-point threshold, providing reliable production in the middle and top of our order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the final utility spot, where **Cole Young** put up a respectable 45.47 efficiency score but ultimately yielded to the superior platoon and park factors surrounding **Zach McKinstry**. While **Cole Young**\u2019s profile is trending upward, the optimizer favored **Zach McKinstry**\u2019s +5% park factor and the current offensive environment against S. Burke. We are also closely monitoring the lineup statuses for **Isaac Paredes**, **Brice Turang**, and **Josh Naylor**; should any of these veterans shift down in their respective batting orders or sit, we will be forced to adjust our efficiency projections downward. With **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, making it critical that **Gabriel Moreno** maintains his recent form against Elder to stabilize our C1 production.",
